# Setting Stop Loss to 1% of Account Balance in MQL5

Here's how to calculate and set a stop loss that represents 1% of your trading balance:

## Basic Calculation

```mql5
double accountBalance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
double riskAmount = accountBalance * 0.01;  // 1% of balance
```

## Complete Example with Order Placement

```mql5
#include <Trade\Trade.mqh>

CTrade trade;

void OnStart()
{
    double symbol_bid = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_BID);
    double symbol_ask = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_ASK);
    double point = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_POINT);
    int digits = (int)SymbolInfoInteger(_Symbol, SYMBOL_DIGITS);

    // Calculate 1% risk amount
    double accountBalance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
    double riskAmount = accountBalance * 0.01;

    // Define lot size (example: fixed or calculated)
    double lotSize = 0.1;

    // BUY ORDER - Calculate Stop Loss
    double buyPrice = symbol_ask;
    double pipValue = point * lotSize * SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
    double stopLossPips = riskAmount / pipValue;
    double buyStopLoss = NormalizeDouble(buyPrice - (stopLossPips * point), digits);

    // Place BUY order
    trade.Buy(lotSize, _Symbol, buyPrice, buyStopLoss, 0, "Buy with 1% SL");

    // SELL ORDER - Calculate Stop Loss
    double sellPrice = symbol_bid;
    double sellStopLoss = NormalizeDouble(sellPrice + (stopLossPips * point), digits);

    // Place SELL order
    trade.Sell(lotSize, _Symbol, sellPrice, sellStopLoss, 0, "Sell with 1% SL");
}
```

## Simplified Function Approach

```mql5
double CalculateStopLoss(double entryPrice, bool isBuy, double lotSize)
{
    double accountBalance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
    double riskAmount = accountBalance * 0.01;  // 1% risk

    double point = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_POINT);
    double tickValue = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
    int digits = (int)SymbolInfoInteger(_Symbol, SYMBOL_DIGITS);

    double pipValue = point * lotSize * tickValue;
    double stopLossPips = riskAmount / pipValue;

    double stopLoss;
    if (isBuy)
        stopLoss = NormalizeDouble(entryPrice - (stopLossPips * point), digits);
    else
        stopLoss = NormalizeDouble(entryPrice + (stopLossPips * point), digits);

    return stopLoss;
}

// Usage:
double buyStopLoss = CalculateStopLoss(1.2500, true, 0.1);
```

## Key Points

| Component | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| `AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE)` | Gets current account balance |
| `0.01` | Represents 1% (change to 0.02 for 2%, etc.) |
| `SYMBOL_POINT` | Smallest price movement |
| `SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE` | Value per pip |
| `NormalizeDouble()` | Rounds to correct decimal places |

## Alternative: Use Risk Percentage Parameter

```mql5
double CalculateStopLossPercent(double entryPrice, bool isBuy, double lotSize, double riskPercent)
{
    double accountBalance = AccountInfoDouble(ACCOUNT_BALANCE);
    double riskAmount = accountBalance * (riskPercent / 100.0);

    double point = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_POINT);
    double tickValue = SymbolInfoDouble(_Symbol, SYMBOL_TRADE_TICK_VALUE);
    int digits = (int)SymbolInfoInteger(_Symbol, SYMBOL_DIGITS);

    double pipValue = point * lotSize * tickValue;
    double stopLossPips = riskAmount / pipValue;

    if (isBuy)
        return NormalizeDouble(entryPrice - (stopLossPips * point), digits);
    else
        return NormalizeDouble(entryPrice + (stopLossPips * point), digits);
}

// Usage for 1%:
double stopLoss = CalculateStopLossPercent(1.2500, true, 0.1, 1.0);
```

This ensures your stop loss is dynamically calculated based on your current balance!

